wharton-muslims-in-business.description:
The mission of the Club is to cultivate a welcoming and engaged community around the Islamic faith, Muslim culture and identity, and the professional and business development of its members. The Club shall serve students with a wide range of relationships to Islam and the Muslim community, including students who:
1. Identify as Muslim or practice Islam;
2. Have family, cultural, or personal ties to Islam or Muslim communities;
3. Intend to work, invest, build businesses, or pursue professional opportunities connected to Muslim communities or markets;
4. Have academic, cultural, or social interests in Islam or the Muslim world; or
5. Simply wish to learn more about and engage with the Muslim community.
Membership and participation shall not require Muslim faith, religious practice, heritage, nationality, citizenship, language ability, or prior experience with Islam or Muslim communities.
